---
import PageShell from '../../../layouts/PageShell.astro';

const title = 'Why KI einfach verstehen exists — KI einfach verstehen';
const description =
	"The story behind KI einfach verstehen: why a simple question about how AI actually works turned into this project.";
---

<PageShell lang="en" title={title} description={description} otherLangHref="/de/warum/" themenHref="/en/#themenbereiche">
	<article class="wrap warum">
		<h1>Why KI einfach verstehen exists</h1>
		<div class="prose">
			<p>
				At the start was actually a pretty simple question: <strong>How does this all actually work?</strong>
			</p>
			<p>
				Like probably a lot of people, we started out just using AI. For writing, for coding, for research, for
				automating things. And a lot of it works surprisingly well, even if you have no idea what's actually
				happening behind the scenes.
			</p>
			<p>At some point, that stopped being enough for us.</p>
			<p>
				What's actually happening inside a language model? What are tokens and parameters? How does a model learn?
				Why can AI handle some things brilliantly and completely fail at others that seem trivial?
			</p>
			<p>
				So we started digging deeper. And we quickly noticed something: there's an overwhelming amount of
				information about AI out there, but getting a real foothold is still surprisingly hard.
			</p>
			<p>
				Many explanations stay on the surface. Others dive straight into the deep end, assuming you already know
				things you probably don't. What we kept missing were the explanations in between: clear enough to actually
				get you started, but thorough enough that you end up understanding <em>why</em> something works, not just
				what it's called.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>That's why KI einfach verstehen exists. We wanted to build exactly what we were missing ourselves.</strong>
			</p>
			<p>
				We're still learning as we go. The deeper we get into a topic, the more new questions come up. Those are
				the questions we try to answer here, one by one, breaking them down so they make sense even without much
				technical background.
			</p>
			<p>
				If you want to understand AI for your job or your everyday life, without having to study computer science
				first, that's exactly where this project comes in.
			</p>
			<p>
				We start with the basics and work our way forward from there, step by step. Not just toward <strong>what</strong> a term means or <strong>what</strong> a model does, but toward <strong>why</strong> it works, and how everything fits together.
			</p>
		</div>
	</article>
</PageShell>

